    "body": "# Community Guidelines\n\nPawsPal works because neighbours trust each other with the animals they love. Every member agrees to these five rules.\n\n## The five rules\n\n### 1. Care for every pet like your own\nFood, water, walks, love and quick updates. Follow the owner's instructions. If something is wrong, tell the owner straight away and get a vet if needed.\n\n### 2. Use real photos only\nYour own face as your profile photo, and your own pets. No filters, sunglasses, group shots, cartoons or stolen images.\n\n### 3. Keep chat in the app until a booking is confirmed\nDon't ask for or share phone numbers, WhatsApp, Instagram, InstaPay, bank details or links before then. The app hides them automatically, and repeated attempts are a rule break. Once you both accept the terms, contact details unlock and you can arrange payment directly with each other.\n\n### 4. Be honest and kind\nIn messages, listings and reviews. Describe your pet and your home truthfully. No harassment, threats, insults or discrimination.\n\n### 5. Report problems\nUse **Report** on any profile, chat or booking. Every report is read by a person. Reporting in good faith never counts against you.\n\n## How we enforce them\n\n| Step | When | What happens |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Reminder** | A first, minor slip (for example a blurry face photo) | A friendly note explaining the rule |\n| **Warning** | A clear break of a rule | Recorded on your account; you are told which rule |\n| **Suspension** | Repeated or serious breaks | Your profile is hidden for 3 days, 7 days or **until fixed**. You see exactly what to fix |\n| **Removal** | Danger to a person or animal, fraud, fake identity, or breaking the rules again after suspension | The account is closed and the person cannot rejoin |\n\nYou can **appeal** any warning, suspension or removal in the app. A person reviews every appeal and replies.\n\n## Zero tolerance\n\nThese lead to immediate removal and, where appropriate, a report to the authorities:\n\n- harming, neglecting or abandoning an animal\n- threats or violence against a person\n- fake identity or someone else's ID\n- selling, breeding or fighting animals through PawsPal\n- fraud or stealing payments\n\n## Safety tips\n\n- Meet in daylight for the first handover, and take the handover photo together.\n- Check the pet's vaccination record and vet contact before the stay.\n- Keep all messages in the app; it protects you if something goes wrong.\n- Use **Safety Center › Emergency** if a pet is ill, injured or lost."
